      "questionName": "tremble, erupt, disaster, funnel, rescue worker, shake",
      "questionType": "FillBlank",
      "questionText": "<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Complete the text, using the words given. You may make any changes to the words if necessary. There is one word you don't need to use.</strong></p>\n<table style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; height: 98px; border-color: #2dc26b; border-style: dashed;\" border=\"1\" cellspacing=\"5\" cellpadding=\"5\">\n<tbody>\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 33.4277%; height: 18px; text-align: center;\"><strong>disaster</strong></td>\n<td style=\"width: 33.4277%; height: 18px; text-align: center;\"><strong>tremble</strong></td>\n<td style=\"width: 33.2872%; height: 18px; text-align: center;\"><strong>involve</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 33.4277%; height: 18px; text-align: center;\"><strong>erupt</strong></td>\n<td style=\"width: 33.4277%; height: 18px; text-align: center;\"><strong>landslide</strong></td>\n<td style=\"width: 33.2872%; height: 18px; text-align: center;\"><strong>funnel</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br>Natural disasters can happen anywhere and often cause great damage to people and the environment. During an earthquake, the ground begins to <strong><span class='fillblank-option'><label>15.1</label><input id='fbo-901645-0' class='ms fillblank-option-15' index='0' name='fbo-901645-0' type='text' size='11' autocomplete='off' data-testid='fillblank-input-901645-0' /></span></strong>.&nbsp;This kind of <strong><span class='fillblank-option'><label>15.2</label><input id='fbo-901645-1' class='ms fillblank-option-15' index='1' name='fbo-901645-1' type='text' size='9' autocomplete='off' data-testid='fillblank-input-901645-1' /></span></strong> can make buildings collapse and leave many people without homes and in need of help. Another dangerous event is a volcanic eruption. When a volcano <strong><span class='fillblank-option'><label>15.3</label><input id='fbo-901645-2' class='ms fillblank-option-15' index='2' name='fbo-901645-2' type='text' size='9' autocomplete='off' data-testid='fillblank-input-901645-2' /></span></strong>, it releases hot lava, ash, and smoke, which can destroy everything in its path. Tornadoes are also very scary. They look like a spinning <strong><span class='fillblank-option'><label>15.4</label><input id='fbo-901645-3' class='ms fillblank-option-15' index='3' name='fbo-901645-3' type='text' size='7' autocomplete='off' data-testid='fillblank-input-901645-3' /></span></strong> in the sky and pull up trees, cars, and even houses. <strong><span class='fillblank-option'><label>15.5</label><input id='fbo-901645-4' class='ms fillblank-option-15' index='4' name='fbo-901645-4' type='text' size='11' autocomplete='off' data-testid='fillblank-input-901645-4' /></span></strong> are another serious natural disaster. The soil and rocks on a hill slide down, block roads, and damage villages. To stay safe, people should prepare by having emergency plans and listening to safety warnings.</p>",
